<http://data.silknow.org/object/edf3395c-1007-392d-a681-4847179a5e51/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Dress fabric of woven silk, twill binding.\nPatterned with a repeating sequence of two narrow stripes.\n[1] black ground with a red and white flower and orange leaf forming a meander with green details.\n[2] white ground with a thin black meander bearing small and much faded violet buds.\nA very narrow black and white stripe edges each wider stripe.\nWarp: black silk and white Z-twist silk.\nWeft: red, green, violet, orange, white and black silk, all Z-twist.\nType possibly known as Hussain Kuli Khan."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/edf3395c-1007-392d-a681-4847179a5e51> .

<https://sws.geonames.org/130758/>
