        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Dress fabric of woven silk, Iran, 1860-1899"@en , "Dress fabric of woven silk, twill binding.\nPatterned with a repeating sequence of two narrow stripes.\n[1] black ground with a red and white flower and orange leaf forming a meander with green details.\n[2] white ground with a thin black meander bearing small and much faded violet buds.\nA very narrow black and white stripe edges each wider stripe.\nWarp: black silk and white Z-twist silk.\nWeft: red, green, violet, orange, white and black silk, all Z-twist.\nType possibly known as Hussain Kuli Khan."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/76baec69-0fc9-3b49-84e5-734a05ebcc87> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/71219c5a-54b5-31a8-b047-be902043f08b> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Dress fabric of woven silk, twill binding.\nPatterned with a repeating sequence of two narrow stripes.\n[1] black ground with a red and white flower and orange leaf forming a meander with green details.\n[2] white ground with a thin black meander bearing small and much faded violet buds.\nA very narrow black and white stripe edges each wider stripe.\nWarp: black silk and white Z-twist silk.\nWeft: red, green, violet, orange, white and black silk, all Z-twist.\nType possibly known as Hussain Kuli Khan."@en , "Dress fabric of woven silk, Iran, 1860-1899"@en ;
